This golden master was generated with GNU tar 1.34 for the POSIX ustar subset
that GNU tar and Abuild's native writer can both encode byte-identically.

Covered entry kinds and layout rules:
- regular file with payload and zero padding
- empty directory with trailing slash
- symbolic link with a short target
- FIFO node
- character and block device nodes with major/minor numbers
- regular file whose path is split into POSIX ustar prefix/name fields

Intentionally not covered here:
- GNU LongName/LongLink metadata records
- PAX records
- Abuild-specific metadata/error handling

Those cases are covered by direct raw-header tests and by reader checks against
GNU tar and libarchive. This fixture exists specifically as an independent
byte-for-byte reference for the standardized POSIX ustar subset.

Generation command used in an abuild-dev container:

  rm -rf /tmp/tar-golden-root /tmp/tar-golden.tar /tmp/tar-golden.hex
  mkdir -p /tmp/tar-golden-root/directory
  cp /work/data/tests_abuild_file_formats_tar/regular_file \
    /tmp/tar-golden-root/regular_file
  ln -s regular_file /tmp/tar-golden-root/symbolic_link
  mkfifo /tmp/tar-golden-root/fifo
  mknod /tmp/tar-golden-root/character_device c 5 12
  mknod /tmp/tar-golden-root/block_device b 21 5
  p=$(printf %0150d 0 | tr 0 a)
  mkdir -p /tmp/tar-golden-root/$p/middle
  cp /work/data/tests_abuild_file_formats_tar/regular_file \
    /tmp/tar-golden-root/$p/middle/leaf.txt
  chmod 0644 /tmp/tar-golden-root/regular_file \
    /tmp/tar-golden-root/$p/middle/leaf.txt
  chmod 0755 /tmp/tar-golden-root/directory
  chmod 0777 /tmp/tar-golden-root/fifo
  chmod 0772 /tmp/tar-golden-root/character_device
  chmod 0006 /tmp/tar-golden-root/block_device
  tar -b1 --format=ustar --owner=0 --group=0 --numeric-owner \
    --mtime=@946684800 -C /tmp/tar-golden-root \
    -cf /tmp/tar-golden.tar \
    regular_file directory symbolic_link fifo character_device block_device \
    $p/middle/leaf.txt
  hexdump -vC /tmp/tar-golden.tar > gnu-ustar-subset.hex

Regenerating the fixture requires privileges for mknod. The unit test itself
uses the committed hex dump and does not need any special privileges.

Reference SHA-256 of /tmp/tar-golden.tar:

  4a57dfbf22f27b4829a79b814342b8efda7e05fb03e5c5930c525f2941cf4bfc
